[{:db/id 17592186198360 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ffd9297-ce86-5e32-becf-cbd84b607c09"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ffd9297-ce86-5e32-becf-cbd84b607c09" :question/id #uuid "9ffd9297-ce86-5e32-becf-cbd84b607c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-160476" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}(u-1)^{3}-(v-2)^{3} \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=(u-1)^{3}-(v-2)^{3}$ and $y(u,v)=u+v.$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =3(u-1)^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-3(v-2)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3(u-1)^{2} & -3(v-2)^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(u-1)^{2}\\cdot 1-(-3(v-2)^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3(u-1)^{2}+3(v-2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 3(u-1)^{2}+3(v-2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3(u-1)^{2}+3(v-2)^{2}=0$ defines the point $(1,2)$ in the $uv$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58f46da7-c0a4-56d1-b636-f9591428aeed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58f46da7-c0a4-56d1-b636-f9591428aeed" :answer-field/id #uuid "58f46da7-c0a4-56d1-b636-f9591428aeed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9eec4e3-df6c-5bff-a85a-74dee074332e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c9ce46f-74e5-51fc-85f1-be6a4dc35d80" "answer-1c1b9805-9295-5f1f-93ad-1b87d622dbf3" "answer-2794a3de-45e3-5d1c-aaa5-e06f453a2bb3" "answer-144c14ba-18af-5f87-a114-1f0e70bc5c73" "answer-c9eec4e3-df6c-5bff-a85a-74dee074332e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c9ce46f-74e5-51fc-85f1-be6a4dc35d80" :answer/id #uuid "0c9ce46f-74e5-51fc-85f1-be6a4dc35d80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the line $v=-u.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c1b9805-9295-5f1f-93ad-1b87d622dbf3" :answer/id #uuid "1c1b9805-9295-5f1f-93ad-1b87d622dbf3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the line $v=2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2794a3de-45e3-5d1c-aaa5-e06f453a2bb3" :answer/id #uuid "2794a3de-45e3-5d1c-aaa5-e06f453a2bb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the line $v=u.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144c14ba-18af-5f87-a114-1f0e70bc5c73" :answer/id #uuid "144c14ba-18af-5f87-a114-1f0e70bc5c73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The only critical point is $(-1,-2).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9eec4e3-df6c-5bff-a85a-74dee074332e" :answer/id #uuid "c9eec4e3-df6c-5bff-a85a-74dee074332e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The only critical point is $(1,2).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9d89a91b-0f23-5034-8485-cf2fdb766717" :activity/id #uuid "9d89a91b-0f23-5034-8485-cf2fdb766717" :activity/title "The Inverse Function Theorem" :activity/